<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chen Gongbo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1892">1892</a>–<a href="/years/1946">1946</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chen Gongbo was a founding member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinese-communist-party">Chinese Communist Party</a> who later joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a> and followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-jingwei">Wang Jingwei</a> into collaboration with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. He served as a leading official of the Japanese-backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanjing">Nanjing</a> government and became its acting head after Wang's death in 1944. He was executed for treason in 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chen-gongbo.jpg" alt="Chen Gongbo" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Chen_Gongbo_cropped.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
